                        THE WAZE COMMUNITY SOURCE LICENSE

A NOTE ON COLLABORATION & LICENSING
I poured a massive amount of time, research, and unique logic into this 
software to help the Waze editing community. I actively welcome and encourage 
contributions, feature requests, and community support! 

- Want to add a feature? Please submit a Pull Request! I'd love to merge your 
  great ideas into the main script so everyone benefits.
- Want to build an extension? Go for it, but please consider contributing your 
  hooks upstream.
- Want to clone this, change the UI colors, and release it as your own? 
  Please don't. 

By using, modifying, or distributing this software, you agree to the following 
terms.

1. DEFINITIONS
"Original Software" refers to the source code, logic, design, and file 
structures authored by the Original Author, regardless of the platform or 
channel from which it was acquired, in whole or in part, including specific 
algorithms and logic routines.

"Original Author" refers to David Slutsky (known as r0den within the Waze
community).

"Modification" refers to any alteration, addition, deletion, or partial 
extraction applied to the Original Software.

"Significant Change" refers to the addition of substantial, novel, 
human-authored logic, features, or bug fixes that directly impact the core 
Waze Map Editor functionality. Cosmetic alterations (e.g., UI color changes, 
renaming variables, code refactoring), bundling the Original Software with 
third-party code, or adding supplementary non-functional features (e.g., 
telemetry, logging, visual themes) do not constitute a Significant Change.

"Extension" refers to a separate script or program that relies on, but does 
not duplicate the core logic of, the Original Software, provided that it does 
not obscure, suppress, or maliciously intercept the user interface, core 
functionality, or attribution elements of the Original Software.

2. PERMISSIONS GRANTED
You are granted the non-exclusive, free-of-charge right to:
2.1. Use: Download, install, and execute the Original Software for the 
     explicit purpose of editing and improving the Waze map.
2.2. Modify: Alter the code for your own private, non-distributed use.
2.3. Fork: Create and maintain a public or private fork of the repository 
     utilizing standard platform features (e.g., GitHub's Fork button) in 
     compliance with the host platform's Terms of Service.

3. RESTRICTIONS ON USE & MONETIZATION
The following restrictions apply universally to all users of the Original 
Software, Modifications, and Extensions, regardless of whether the software is 
publicly distributed or kept private:
3.1. Scope of Use: You may freely use the software for the explicit purpose of 
     editing and improving the Waze map. Indirect commercial benefits derived 
     from utilizing the improved map data are permitted. You may not use the 
     Original Software or its underlying logic for any purpose outside of this 
     specific scope (e.g., building standalone commercial routing tools, data 
     scraping).
3.2. Strict Non-Commercialization: You may not extract, distribute, monetize, 
     or leverage the software's codebase, Modifications, or Extensions for any 
     direct or indirect commercial advantage. This strictly prohibits 
     monetizing the software through any means whatsoever, including but not 
     limited to: selling licenses, paywalls, subscriptions, advertising, 
     sponsored links, or data selling. 
3.3. No Solicitation: You may not solicit voluntary donations, tips, or 
     sponsorships (e.g., Patreon, "Buy Me a Coffee") within the software's 
     user interface, source code comments, primary distribution pages, or on 
     any secondary pages, documentation sites, support channels, or 
     promotional materials connected to the software, Modification, or 
     Extension. General, project-agnostic donation links located on a 
     developer's global user profile (e.g., a standard GitHub Sponsors button) 
     are permitted, provided those links are not actively solicited, directed 
     to, or explicitly connected to the distribution or support of this 
     software. The software itself must remain completely financially untethered.

4. RESTRICTIONS ON DISTRIBUTION
Unmodified Redistribution: You may not re-upload, host, or distribute exact, 
unmodified copies of the Original Software on any external public platform, 
directory, or repository (e.g., GreasyFork). Platform-native forks (e.g., on 
GitHub) are permitted under Clause 2.3, but may not be actively distributed or 
promoted as standalone releases.

Modified & Extension Distribution: You may not distribute, publish, or share 
Modified versions or Extensions of the Original Software unless ALL of the 
following conditions are met:
4.1. Significant Changes Required: Your Modification must contain Significant 
     Changes. You may not distribute slightly modified clones, partial 
     extractions, or cosmetic tweaks of the Original Software. Furthermore, 
     the inclusion of a Significant Change does not legitimize or grant 
     permission to bundle the Original Software with plagiarized or 
     unauthorized third-party code. 
4.2. AI and Automated Derivatives: Utilizing Artificial Intelligence, Large 
     Language Models (LLMs), or other automated tools to refactor, translate, 
     or modify the Original Software does not break the chain of copyright or 
     grant original authorship over the resulting code. Under the terms of 
     this license, any output generated by processing the Original Software 
     through such tools shall be treated as a Modification and remains fully 
     bound by all restrictions herein.

5. ATTRIBUTION & ENDORSEMENT REQUIREMENTS
If you distribute a permitted Modification or Extension, you must comply with 
the following: 
5.1. Publication Channels: If the software is published on a public forum, 
     platform, or directory (e.g., Waze Discuss, GreasyFork, GitHub), the 
     publication description must explicitly name the Original Author (r0den
     for Waze-related platforms, or David Slutsky elsewhere) and include a
     direct hyperlink to the Original Software's repository.
5.2. In-Script Attribution: The script's user interface or metadata block must 
     retain a visible credit acknowledging the Original Author of the core 
     logic. 
5.3. Modification Notice & No Endorsement: You must prominently state within 
     the software and its distribution page that the software has been 
     modified from the original. You may not imply or state that the Original 
     Author endorses, maintains, or is in any way responsible for your 
     modified version or any map damages it may cause.

